# Line endings are part of this project's provenance.
#
# `behavior/spec.yaml` is hashed byte-for-byte, and that hash is pinned inside
# the frozen Dataset V1 record, the prompt-ceiling manifest and 18 result
# artifacts (`dc14f40b94d622d1...`). With `core.autocrlf` deciding endings per
# machine, the same unchanged spec hashes differently on different checkouts,
# silently severing every result from the behavior it claims to measure. This
# was observed: a fresh checkout produced `6359a71245432547...` for a file git
# reported as unmodified.
#
# Pinning the ending makes the hash a property of the content again. The rule is
# deliberately narrow — no repo-wide normalization, which would rewrite every
# working file for no benefit.
#
# `tests/test_training_integration.py` fails if this ever stops holding.
behavior/spec.yaml text eol=crlf
